The most portable solution is to make the memory validity a precondition rather than a postulate inside the runner.                                                    
                                                                                                                                                                         
  Currently:                                                                                                                                                             
  -- Postulate inside fst-runner                                                                                                                                         
  postulate                                                                                                                                                              
    fst-mem-valid : ∀ σ s → StateCorresponds σ s →                                                                                                                       
      ∃[ fst-loc ] (readLoc σ (readReg RDI) ≡ just fst-loc)                                                                                                              
                                                                                                                                                                         
  fst-runner : IRRunner fst-ir                                                                                                                                           
  fst-runner ... = ... fst-mem-valid σ s sc ...                                                                                                                          
                                                                                                                                                                         
  Portable approach:                                                                                                                                                     
  -- fst-runner takes the proof as a parameter                                                                                                                           
  fst-runner : ∀ {A B} (fst-loc : ValueLocation FS') →                                                                                                                   
    (mem-valid : ∀ σ s → StateCorresponds σ s →                                                                                                                          
      readLoc σ (readReg RDI) ≡ just fst-loc) →                                                                                                                          
    IRRunner (fst-ir {A} {B})                                                                                                                                            
                                                                                                                                                                         
  Then ir-runner (which builds IRRunner by induction) also takes a validity parameter:                                                                                   
  ir-runner : ∀ {A B} (ir : IR A B) →                                                                                                                                    
    InputValid ir →  -- Abstract predicate, instantiated at integration                                                                                                  
    IRRunner ir                                                                                                                                                          
                                                                                                                                                                         
  Why this is most portable:                                                                                                                                             
  1. Layer 1→2 stays pure - No assumptions about where validity comes from                                                                                               
  2. Backend-agnostic - Different backends can provide validity proofs differently                                                                                       
  3. Testable - Tests can construct validity proofs directly                                                                                                             
  4. Clean integration - At the full-correctness theorem, we instantiate with ValidAtWF from Layer 2→3                                                                   
                                                                                                                                                                         
  The pattern: Push proof obligations to the caller, don't hide them in postulates. The postulate becomes explicit in the type signature, making the contract clear.     
                                                                                                                                                                         
